 características de seguridad","fr":"Navi est un langage de programmation compilé haute performance avec typage statique et fonctionnalités de sécurité","de":"Navi ist eine kompilierte Hochleistungs-Programmiersprache mit statischer Typisierung und Sicherheitsfunktionen","pt":"O que é Navi? Uma linguagem de programação de alto desempenho, estáticamente tipada e compilada.","ru":"Что такое Navi? Высокопроизводительный язык программирования, статически типизированный и компилируемый.","ar":"ما هي نافي؟ لغة برمجة عالية الأداء، محوسبة بشكل ثابت ومجمّعة."},"features":{"en":["Statically typed with type inference for reliable code execution","No NULL pointer exceptions for enhanced code stability","Modern optional types similar to Rust''s Option for flexible coding","Comprehensive error handling with throws, try, try?, and try! for robust error management","Built-in support for script-like execution with compiled performance comparable to Go, Rust, and C"],"zh":["静态类型以确保类型安全","现代可选类型以处理空值","综合错误处理以确保代码可靠性","编译后的性能与 Go、Rust 和 C 相比","脚本式执行以提高开发效率"],"ja":["静的型付けによる型安全性の確保","モダンなオプショナル型による null 値の処理","包括的なエラーハンドリングによるコードの信頼性の確保","コンパイル後のパフォーマンスは Go、Rust、C と比較可能","スクリプトのような実行による開発効率の向上"],"ko":["정적 타이핑을 통한 타입 안전성 보장","모던 옵셔널 타입을 통한 널 값 처리","포괄적인 오류 처리를 통한 코드 신뢰성 보장","컴파일된 성능은 Go, Rust, C와 비교 가능","스크립트와 유사한 실행을 통한 개발 효율성 향상"],"es":["Tipado estático con inferencia de tipos","Sin excepciones de punteros NULL","Manejo de errores robusto con throws, try, try? y try!","Tipos opcionales modernos similares a Rust''s Option","Ejecución de scripts con rendimiento comparable a Go, Rust y C"],"fr":["Typage statique avec inférence de types","Pas d''exceptions de pointeurs NULL","Gestion d''erreurs robuste avec throws, try, try? et try!","Types optionnels modernes similaires à Rust''s Option","Exécution de scripts avec des performances comparables à Go, Rust et C"],"de":["Statische Typisierung mit Typinferenz","Keine NULL-Pointer-Ausnahmen","Robuste Fehlerbehandlung mit throws, try, try? und try!","Moderne optionale Typen ähnlich wie Rust''s Option","Skriptausführung mit Leistungen vergleichbar mit Go, Rust und C"],"pt":["Tipagem estática com inferência de tipo","Sem exceções de ponteiro nulo","Execução de script com desempenho compilado","Tipos opcionais modernos","Tratamento de erros abrangente com throws, try, try? e try!"],"ru":["Статическая типизация с выводом типа","Нет исключений нулевого указателя","Выполнение скрипта с компилируемой производительностью","Современные необязательные типы","Полное xử lý ошибок с throws, try, try? и try!"],"ar":["التنميط الثابت مع استنتاج النوع","بدون استثناءات للمؤشرات الفارغة","تنفيذ البرمجيات بأداء مجمّع","أنواع اختيارية حديثة","معالجة الأخطاء الشاملة مع throws و try و try? و try!"]},"keywords":{"en":["how to use navi","what is navi","navi alternative","navi vs rust","navi install","navi setup guide","navi programming language","statically-typed language","compiled language"],"zh":["Navi 编程语言","静态类型编程语言","高性能编程语言","现代可选类型","综合错误处理","编译后的性能","AI 编程工具","AIエージェント"],"ja":["Navi プログラミング言語","静的型付けプログラミング言語","高性能プログラミング言語","モダンなオプショナル型","包括的なエラーハンドリング","コンパイル後のパフォーマンス","AI プログラミングツール","AIエージェント"],"ko":["Navi 프로그래밍 언어","정적 타이핑 프로그래밍 언어","고성능 프로그래밍 언어","모던 옵셔널 타입","포괄적인 오류 처리","컴파일된 성능","AI 프로그래밍 도구","AI 에이전트"],"es":["Navi lenguaje de programación","lenguajes de programación compilados","tipado estático","manejo de errores","programación de alto rendimiento","desarrollo de software","Herramientas de desarrollo","Agentes de IA","Herramientas de código"],"fr":["Navi langage de programmation","langages de programmation compilés","typage statique","gestion d''erreurs","programmation haute performance","développement de logiciels","Outils de développement","Agents d''IA","Outils de code"],"de":["Navi Programmiersprache","kompilierte Programmiersprachen","statische Typisierung","Fehlerbehandlung","Hochleistungs-Programmierung","Software-Entwicklung","Entwicklungstools","KI-Agents","Code-Tools"],"pt":["linguagem de programação navi","desenvolvimento de software","programação de alto desempenho","tipagem estática","execução de script","erros de ponteiro nulo","opções de tratamento de erros"],"ru":["язык программирования navi","разработка программного обеспечения","высокопроизводительное программирование","статическая типизация","выполнение скрипта","ошибки нулевого указателя","варианты обработки ошибок"],"ar":["لغة برمجة نافي","تطوير البرمجيات","برمجةعالية الأداء","التنميط الثابت","تنفيذ البرمجيات","أخطاء المؤشرات الفارغة","خيارات معالجة الأخطاء"]}},"owner":"navi-language","repo":"navi","repoPath":"navi-language/navi","stars":104,"forks":1,"updatedAt":"2026-01-21T12:05:11Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"navi","description":"Navi programming language expert. Use when writing Navi code, implementing features, handling errors, or working with Navis type system, concurrency, and modules. Navi is a high-performance, statically-typed compiled language with modern optional types, no NULL pointer exceptions, and built-in concurrency support.","bodyPreview":"# Navi Language Skill\n\nNavi (/ˈnævi/) is a high-performance, statically-typed compiled language designed for complex computing tasks. It offers script-like execution with compiled performance comparable to Go, Rust, and C.\n\n## Core Characteristics\n\n- **Statically typed** with type inference\n- **No NULL pointer exceptions** - once compiled, code runs reliably\n- **Modern optional types** (similar to Rust''s Option)\n- **Comprehensive error handling** with `throws`, `try`, `try?`, `try!`\n- **Built-in","body":"# Navi Language Skill\n\nNavi (/ˈnævi/) is a high-performance, statically-typed compiled language designed for complex computing tasks. It offers script-like execution with compiled performance comparable to Go, Rust, and C.\n\n## Core Characteristics\n\n- **Statically typed** with type inference\n- **No NULL pointer exceptions** - once compiled, code runs reliably\n- **Modern optional types** (similar to Rust''s Option)\n- **Comprehensive error handling** with `throws`, `try`, `try?`, `try!`\n- **Built-in concurrency** with `spawn` and channels (single-threaded concurrency)\n- **Cross-platform**: Linux, Windows, macOS, WebAssembly\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n### Basic Syntax\n\n```nv\n// Entry point (main must have throws)\nfn main() throws {\n    let name = \"World\";\n    let message = `Hello ${name}.`;  // String interpolation\n    println(message);  // Auto-imported from std.io\n}\n\n// Functions\nfn add(a: int, b: int): int {\n    return a + b;\n}\n\n// Structs\nstruct User {\n    name: string,\n    email: string?,  // Optional field\n    active: bool = true,  // Default value\n}\n\nimpl User {\n    fn new(name: string): User {\n        return User { name, email: nil };\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Key Syntax Rules\n\n- Statements end with `;`\n- Use 4 spaces for indentation\n- `//` for single-line comments, `///` for doc comments\n- String interpolation uses backticks: `` `value: ${x}` ``\n- File extension: `.nv`\n\n### Important Syntax Limitations\n\n**If and Switch are STATEMENTS, not expressions:**\n```nv\n// ❌ WRONG - Cannot assign if/switch directly\nlet status = if (active) { \"on\" } else { \"off\" };\nlet day = switch (n) { case 1: \"Mon\"; default: \"Other\"; };\n\n// ✅ CORRECT - Use statements, then assign\nlet status = \"\";\nif (active) {\n    status = \"on\";\n} else {\n    status = \"off\";\n}\n```\n\n**Scientific notation requires explicit sign:**\n```nv\n// ❌ WRONG\nlet num = 1.5e10;\n\n// ✅ CORRECT\nlet num = 1.5e+10;  // or 1.5e-10 for negative exponent\n```\n\n**Map access with `[]` vs `.get()`:**\n```nv\nlet scores = {\"Alice\": 95, \"Bob\": 87};\n\n// ❌ WRONG - scores[\"key\"] returns non-optional, can''t use ||\nlet score = scores[\"Eve\"] || 0;\n\n// ✅ CORRECT - Use .get() which returns optional type\nlet score = scores.get(\"Eve\") || 0;\n\n// ✅ Also correct - Direct access (but key must exist)\nlet alice_score = scores[\"Alice\"];  // OK if key exists\n\n// ✅ Also correct - Check before access\nif (scores.get(\"Eve\") != nil) {\n    let score = scores[\"Eve\"];\n}\n```\n\n### Type System Essentials\n\n```nv\n// Primitives (all 64-bit)\nlet n: int = 100;\nlet f: float = 3.14;\nlet b: bool = true;\nlet s: string = \"text\";  // Immutable UTF-8\nlet c: char = ''🎉'';\n\n// Optional types (key to NULL safety)\nlet value: string? = nil;\nlet result = value || \"default\";  // Unwrap or default\nlet length = value?.len();  // Safe chaining (returns nil if value is nil)\nprintln(value!);  // Unwrap (panics if nil - use sparingly)\n\n// Collections\nlet array = [1, 2, 3];\nlet map = {\"key\": \"value\"};\nlet empty: [int] = [];\n```\n\n### Error Handling Pattern\n\n```nv\n// Declare function can throw\nfn divide(a: int, b: int): int throws {\n    if (b == 0) {\n        throw \"Division by zero\";\n    }\n    return a / b;\n}\n\n// Handle errors\nlet result = try? divide(10, 0);  // Returns int? (nil on error)\nlet result = try divide(10, 2);   // Propagate error up\nlet result = try! divide(10, 2);  // Panic on error\n\n// Do-catch block\ndo {\n    let r = try divide(10, 0);\n} catch (e) {\n    println(e.error());\n}\n```\n\n### Control Flow Patterns\n\n```nv\n// If-let for optionals\nif (let value = optional) {\n    println(value);  // value is unwrapped here\n}\n\n// Let-else for early returns\nlet value = optional else {\n    return;\n};\n// value is unwrapped here\n\n// Switch with type matching\nswitch (let v = value.(type)) {\n    case int:\n        println(\"integer\");\n    case string:\n        println(\"string\");\n    default:\n        println(\"other\");\n}\n\n// For loops\nfor (let i in 0..10) {  // Range\n    println(`${i}`);\n}\n\nfor (let item in array) {  // Array\n    println(item);\n}\n\nfor (let k, v in map) {  // Map\n    println(`${k}: ${v}`);\n}\n```\n\n### Concurrency Basics\n\n```nv\nuse std.time;\n\nfn main() throws {\n    let ch = channel::<int>();\n\n    // Spawn concurrent task (not parallel - single thread)\n    spawn {\n        time.sleep(0.1.seconds());\n        try! ch.send(42);\n    }\n\n    let result = try ch.recv();\n    println(`${result}`);\n}\n```\n\n### Worker Pattern\n\n```nv\nuse std.worker.Worker;\n\nfn main() throws {\n    // Create worker with closure\n    let worker = try Worker.create(|worker| {\n        let msg = try worker.recv::<string>()!;\n        try worker.send(msg.to_uppercase());\n    });\n\n    try worker.send(\"hello\");\n    let response = try worker.recv::<string>();\n    println(response);  // \"HELLO\"\n}\n```\n\n### Navi Stream Integration\n\n```nv\nuse nvs.macd;  // Import .nvs file as module\n\nfn main() throws {\n    // Create instance of NVS indicator\n    let indicator = macd.new();\n\n    // Execute with market data\n    indicator.execute(\n        time: 1234567890,\n        open: 100.0,\n        high: 105.0,\n        low: 99.0,\n        close: 103.0,\n        volume: 1000.0,\n        turnover: 100000.0\n    );\n\n    // Access exported variables\n    println(`hist=${indicator.hist:?}`);\n    println(`signal=${indicator.signal:?}`);\n    println(`macd=${indicator.macd:?}`);\n}\n```\n\n### Variadic Arguments\n\n```nv\n// Accept arbitrary number of arguments\nfn sum(values: ..int): int {\n    let total = 0;\n    for (let n in values) {\n        total += n;\n    }\n    return total;\n}\n\nsum(1, 2, 3);           // Call with multiple args\nlet nums = [2, 3, 4];\nsum(..nums);            // Spread array\nsum(1, ..nums, 5);      // Mix regular and spread\n\n// With other parameters\nfn format(prefix: string, parts: ..string): string {\n    return prefix + parts.join(\",\");\n}\n```\n\n## Common Patterns\n\n### Safe Optional Handling\n\n```nv\n// Pattern 1: Unwrap or default\nlet name = user?.name || \"Unknown\";\n\n// Pattern 2: If-let\nif (let user = optional_user) {\n    process(user);\n}\n\n// Pattern 3: Let-else (early return)\nlet user = optional_user else {\n    return;\n};\nprocess(user);\n\n// Pattern 4: Method chaining\nlet email = user?.profile?.email || \"none\";\n```\n\n### Resource Management\n\n```nv\nfn process_file(path: string) throws {\n    let file = try open_file(path);\n\n    defer {\n        file.close();  // Always runs when function exits\n    }\n\n    try file.read();\n    // defer executes here (LIFO if multiple defer blocks)\n}\n```\n\n### Builder Pattern\n\n```nv\nimpl Config {\n    fn new(): Config {\n        return Config { /* defaults */ };\n    }\n\n    fn with_port(self, port: int): Config {\n        self.port = port;\n        return self;\n    }\n}\n\nlet config = Config.new().with_port(8080);\n```\n\n## CLI Commands\n\n```shell\nnavi run              # Run main.nv\nnavi run file.nv      # Run specific file\nnavi test             # Run all tests\nnavi test file.nv     # Run tests in file\nnavi test --doc       # Run doc tests\nnavi build            # Build project\nnavi compile          # Show bytecode\n```\n\n## Testing\n\n````nv\ntest \"addition\" {\n    let result = add(2, 3);\n    assert result == 5;\n    assert_eq result, 5;\n    assert_ne result, 0;\n}\n\n/// Doc test example\n/// ```nv\n/// assert_eq add(1, 2), 3;\n/// ```\nfn add(a: int, b: int): int {\n    return a + b;\n}\n````\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### Naming Conventions\n\n- `snake_case`: variables, functions, fields (`user_name`, `get_user`)\n- `CamelCase`: types, structs, enums (`User`, `HttpRequest`)\n- `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE`: constants (`MAX_SIZE`)\n\n### When to Use Each Error Handler\n\n- `try` - When error should propagate up (most common)\n- `try?` - When failure is acceptable, convert to optional\n- `try!` - When failure is unexpected (use sparingly)\n- `do-catch` - When you need custom error handling logic\n\n### Optional Type Guidelines\n\n- Use `||` for simple defaults\n- Use `?.` for safe chaining\n- Prefer `if let` for conditional logic\n- Use `let else` for early returns\n\n### Concurrency Notes\n\n- `spawn` is **concurrent, not parallel** (single-threaded)\n- Tasks interleave but don''t run simultaneously\n- Use channels for communication between tasks\n- Blocking operations block entire runtime\n\n## When to Load References\n\nLoad reference files when you need detailed information:\n\n- **syntax.md** - Full syntax reference with all language constructs\n- **types.md** - Complete type system including interfaces, unions, type aliases\n- **error-handling.md** - Comprehensive error handling patterns and custom errors\n- **concurrency.md** - Advanced concurrency patterns, channels, and spawn details\n- **modules.md** - Module system, imports, visibility rules\n- **testing.md** - Testing framework, annotations, doc tests\n- **patterns.md** - Common idiomatic patterns and anti-patterns\n\nUse `Read` tool to load these files from `~/.claude/skills/navi/references/` when needed.\n\n## Resources\n\n- **Official Site**: https://navi-lang.org\n- **Standard Library**: https://navi-lang.org/stdlib/\n- **GitHub**: https://github.com/navi-language/navi\n- **Installation**: `curl -sSL https://navi-lang.org/install | sh`\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-06T06:31:10.800Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for High-Performance Agents requiring compiled language execution with modern optional types and comprehensive error handling","zh":"适用于需要编译语言执行的高性能代理，具有现代可选类型和全面的错误处理","ja":"高性能エージェントに適しており、コンパイル言語の実行とモダンなオプショナル型および包括的なエラーハンドリングが可能","ko":"컴파일 언어 실행과 현대적인 옵셔널 타입 및 포괄적인 에러 처리가 필요한 고성능 에이전트에 적합","es":"Ideal para agentes de alto rendimiento que requieren ejecución de lenguaje compilado con tipos opcionales modernos y manejo de errores completo","fr":"Idéal pour les agents haute performance nécessitant l''exécution de langage compilé avec des types optionnels modernes et une gestion des erreurs complète","de":"Ideal für Hochleistungsagenten, die eine Ausführung von Compiliercode mit modernen optionalen Typen und umfassender Fehlerbehandlung erfordern","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Alto Desempenho que exigem execução de linguagem compilada com tipos opcionais modernos e tratamento de erros abrangente","ru":"Идеально для агентов с высокими показателями производительности, требующих выполнения скомпилированного языка с современными необязательными типами и комплексным обработкой ошибок","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء ذوي الأداء العالي الذين يتطلبون تنفيذ لغة مجمعة مع أنواع اختيارية حديثة ومعالجة شاملة للأخطاء"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to execute complex computing tasks with reliability and efficiency, utilizing statically-typed compilation, NULL pointer exception prevention, and built-in comprehensive error handling with throws, try, try?, and try! protocols","zh":"赋予代理执行复杂计算任务的能力，具有可靠性和高效性，利用静态类型编译、NULL指针异常防止和内置的全面错误处理，使用throws、try、try?和try!协议","ja":"エージェントに複雑な計算タスクを実行する能力を与え、信頼性と効率性を提供する。静的型付けのコンパイル、NULLポインタ例外防止、およびビルトインの包括的なエラーハンドリングを使用し、throws、try、try?、try!プロトコルを利用","ko":"에이전트가 복잡한 계산 작업을 실행할 수 있는 능력을 부여하여 신뢰성과 효율성을 제공한다. 정적 타입 컴파일, NULL 포인터 예외 방지 및 내장 포괄적인 에러 처리를 사용하며 throws, try, try?, try! 프로토콜을 활용","es":"Permite a los agentes ejecutar tareas de computación complejas con confiabilidad y eficiencia, utilizando compilación estáticamente tipada, prevención de excepciones de punteros NULL y un manejo de errores integral con protocolos de throws, try, try? y try!","fr":"Permet aux agents d''exécuter des tâches de calcul complexes avec fiabilité et efficacité, en utilisant une compilation statiquement typée, une prévention d''exceptions de pointeurs NULL et une gestion des erreurs complète avec des protocoles de throws, try, try? et try!","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, komplexe Rechenaufgaben mit Zuverlässigkeit und Effizienz auszuführen, indem sie eine statisch typisierte Kompilierung, eine Verhinderung von NULL-Pointer-Ausnahmen und eine umfassende Fehlerbehandlung mit throws-, try-, try?- und try!-Protokollen verwenden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a executar tarefas de computação complexas com confiabilidade e eficiência, utilizando compilação estática, prevenção de exceções de ponteiro nulo e tratamento de erros abrangente com protocolos throws, try, try? e try!","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью выполнять сложные вычислительные задачи с надежностью и эффективностью, используя статическую компиляцию, предотвращение исключений нулевого указателя и встроенное комплексное обработание ошибок с протоколами throws, try, try? и try!","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من تنفيذ مهام الحوسبة المعقدة مع الموثوقية والكفاءة، باستخدام الترجمة الستاتيكية وتجنب استثناءات المؤشرات الفارغة ومعالجة الأخطاء الشاملة بروتوكولات throws وtry وtry? وtry!"},"useCases":{"en":["Compiling high-performance applications with script-like execution","Building reliable systems with modern optional types similar to Rust''s Option","Implementing comprehensive error handling mechanisms with try and throws"],"zh":["编译具有脚本式执行的高性能应用","使用类似Rust的Option的现代可选类型构建可靠的系统","使用try和throws实现全面错误处理机制"],"ja":["スクリプトのような実行を可能とする高性能アプリケーションのコンパイル","RustのOptionに似たモダンなオプショナル型を使用して信頼性の高いシステムを構築","tryとthrowsを使用して包括的なエラーハンドリングメカニズムを実装"],"ko":["스크립트와 같은 실행을 가능하게 하는 고성능 애플리케이션을 컴파일","Rust의 Option과 같은 현대적인 옵셔널 타입을 사용하여 신뢰할 수 있는 시스템을 구축","try와 throws를 사용하여 포괄적인 에러 처리 메커니즘을 구현"],"es":["Compilación de aplicaciones de alto rendimiento con ejecución similar a scripts","Construcción de sistemas confiables con tipos opcionales modernos similares a Rust''s Option","Implementación de mecanismos de manejo de errores completos con try y throws"],"fr":["Compilation d''applications haute performance avec exécution similaire à des scripts","Conception de systèmes fiables avec des types optionnels modernes similaires à Rust''s Option","Mise en œuvre de mécanismes de gestion des erreurs complets avec try et throws"],"de":["Kompilierung von Hochleistungsanwendungen mit skriptähnlicher Ausführung","Aufbau von zuverlässigen Systemen mit modernen optionalen Typen ähnlich wie Rust''s Option","Implementierung von umfassenden Fehlerbehandlungsmechanismen mit try und throws"],"pt":["Compilar aplicações de alto desempenho com execução semelhante a script","Construir sistemas confiáveis com tipos opcionais modernos semelhantes ao Option do Rust","Implementar mecanismos de tratamento de erros abrangentes com try e throws"],"ru":["Компилировать приложения с высокими показателями производительности со сценарием подобной выполнением","Построить надежные системы с современными необязательными типами, аналогичными Option в Rust","Реализовать комплексные механизмы обработки ошибок с помощью try и throws"],"ar":["تجميع تطبيقات الأداء العالي مع تنفيذ شبيه بالسكريبت","بناء أنظمة موثوقة مع أنواع اختيارية حديثة مشابهة لخيار Rust","تنفيذ آليات معالجة الأخطاء الشاملة باستخدام try وthrows"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires compilation before execution","Statically-typed language may require additional type definitions"],"zh":["需要在执行前编译","静态类型语言可能需要额外的类型定义"],"ja":["実行前にコンパイルが必要","静的型付け言語では追加の型定義が必要になる場合がある"],"ko":["실행 전에 컴파일이 필요","정적 타입 언어의 경우 추가적인 타입 정의가 필요할 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere compilación antes de la ejecución","El lenguaje estáticamente tipado puede requerir definiciones de tipo adicionales"],"fr":["Nécessite une compilation avant l''exécution","Le langage statiquement typé peut nécessiter des définitions de type supplémentaires"],"de":["Erfordert eine Kompilierung vor der Ausführung","Die statisch typisierte Sprache kann zusätzliche Typdefinitionen erfordern"],"pt":["Exige compilação antes da execução","Linguagem estática pode exigir definições de tipo adicionais"],"ru":["Требует компиляции перед выполнением","Статически-типизированный язык может требовать дополнительных определений типов"],"ar":["يتطلب تجميعًا قبل التنفيذ","يمكن أن يتطلب لغة σταتيك تعريفات أنواع إضافية"]},"version":4},"contentHash":"348abd78a506026ec4294771db45a29380d6ff856dfae313a209d8d209333848","qualityScore":64}');
